  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Tenant & Identity",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Tenant",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.tenantId) { pm.collectionVariables.set('tenant_id', body.tenantId); }",
                  "pm.test('201/200 and tenantId present', () => { pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code); pm.expect(body.tenantId).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tenants",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tenants"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Tenant\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Exempt (bootstrapping). TenantService.CreateTenant."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Tenants",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tenants",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tenants"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exempt (registry read). TenantService.ListTenants."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Tenant",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tenants/{{tenant_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tenants",
                "{{tenant_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exempt (registry read). TenantService.GetTenant."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create User (agent login)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.userId) { pm.collectionVariables.set('user_id', body.userId); }",
                  "pm.test('201/200 and userId present', () => { pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code); pm.expect(body.userId).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tenants/{{tenant_id}}/users",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tenants",
                "{{tenant_id}}",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"agent1\",\n  \"password\": \"AgentPass123!\",\n  \"roles\": [\"agent\"]\n}"
            },
            "description": "Exempt (bootstrapping). IdentityService.CreateUser. Run 'Create Tenant' first to set {{tenant_id}}.\n\nThe resulting user_id should be reused as the Task Router agent_id in 'Create Agent' below -- see this repo's GAPS.md entry on Agent<->User reconciliation for why that convention matters today."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.token) { pm.collectionVariables.set('jwt', body.token); }",
                  "pm.test('200 and token present', () => { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200); pm.expect(body.token).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"tenantId\": \"{{tenant_id}}\",\n  \"username\": \"agent1\",\n  \"password\": \"AgentPass123!\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Exempt (bootstrapping). IdentityService.Login. Sets {{jwt}}, used as the Bearer token by every 'required'-auth request in this collection via the collection-level auth setting."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get User",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/users/{{user_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{user_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Required auth. IdentityService.GetUser."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/users",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Required auth. IdentityService.ListUsers."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Task Router - Admin Registries",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register Queue",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/queues",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "queues"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"queueId\": \"{{queue_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterAdminService.RegisterQueue. Must exist before EnqueueTask/CreateAgent reference it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Queues",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/queues",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "queues"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Queue",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/queues/{{queue_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "queues",
                "{{queue_id}}"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/statuses",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "statuses"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"Available\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterAdminService.RegisterStatus. NOTE: 'Available' and 'Offline' and 'Not Responding' have spec-level significance (see TASK_ROUTER_SPECIFICATION.md) but are NOT auto-registered -- register any status value you intend to SetAgentStatus to."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Statuses",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/statuses",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "statuses"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register Attribute",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/attributes",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "attributes"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"vip\",\n  \"type\": \"ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_BOOLEAN\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterAdminService.RegisterAttribute. type is one of ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_NUMERIC / ATTRIBUTE_TYPE_BOOLEAN."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Attributes",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/attributes",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "attributes"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Attribute",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/admin/attributes/vip",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "admin",
                "attributes",
                "vip"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Register Queue/Status/Attribute create the resources \"3. Task Router - Agents\" and \"4. Task Router - Tasks & Reservations\" depend on (a queue named {{queue_id}}, an \"Available\" status, a \"vip\" attribute). This folder deliberately does NOT include Remove* requests -- those moved to folder \"7. Cleanup (standalone, run last)\" so a full sequential 1-through-5 run never deletes a resource an earlier step still needs."
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Task Router - Agents",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create Agent",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.agentId) { pm.collectionVariables.set('agent_id', body.agentId); }",
                  "pm.test('201/200 and agentId present', () => { pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code); pm.expect(body.agentId).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"agentId\": \"{{user_id}}\",\n  \"status\": \"Available\",\n  \"capacity\": {\n    \"chat\": { \"ready\": true, \"max\": 1, \"interruptible\": true }\n  },\n  \"queues\": [\"{{queue_id}}\"],\n  \"userId\": \"{{user_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.CreateAgent.\n\nagentId defaults to {{user_id}} (the Tenant & Identity user created earlier) so Agent Presence's WebSocket sub-claim mapping works out of the box -- see GAPS.md's Agent<->User reconciliation entry.\n\nuserId (proto field) is a separate, purely-informational link added 2026-09-13 -- also set to {{user_id}} here, but note it is NOT what Agent Presence's WebSocket mapping actually uses (that's still the JWT sub claim == agentId path, not this field)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Agents",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Agent",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Set Agent Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/status",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "status"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"Available\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.SetAgentStatus. status must already be registered (see 'Register Status')."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Replace Agent Capacity",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/capacity",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "capacity"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"capacity\": {\n    \"chat\": { \"ready\": true, \"max\": 2, \"interruptible\": true }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.ReplaceAgentCapacity. Full replacement map -- omitted channels are removed."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Toggle Channel Ready",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/capacity/chat/toggle",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "capacity",
                "chat",
                "toggle"
              ]
            },
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"ready\": false\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.ToggleChannelReady. {channel} path segment (here 'chat') selects which capacity entry."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Replace Agent Queues",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/queues",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "queues"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"queues\": [\"{{queue_id}}\"]\n}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Replace Agent Attributes",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/attributes",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "attributes"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"attributes\": {\n    \"vip\": { \"isBool\": true, \"boolValue\": true }\n  }\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.ReplaceAgentAttributes. Attribute name(s) must already be registered (see 'Register Attribute')."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Agent Pending Offers",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/offers",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "offers"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.ListAgentPendingOffers. Use this to find {{reservation_id}} after enqueuing a task that matches this agent."
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Delete Agent is NOT included in this folder -- it moved to folder 7 (Cleanup), since deleting the agent here would leave no Available agent for folder 4 (Tasks & Reservations) / folder 5 (Digital Channels Gateway webhook) to match against."
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Task Router - Tasks & Reservations",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Enqueue Task",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.taskId) { pm.collectionVariables.set('task_id', body.taskId); }",
                  "pm.test('201/200 and taskId present', () => { pm.expect([200,201]).to.include(pm.response.code); pm.expect(body.taskId).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tasks",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tasks"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"queueId\": \"{{queue_id}}\",\n  \"taskType\": \"chat\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.EnqueueTask. Prefer 'Digital Channels Gateway > Inbound Chat Webhook' to create a task the same way a real channel would -- this request is here for direct Task Router testing without a channel in the loop."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Tasks",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tasks",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tasks"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Task",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tasks/{{task_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tasks",
                "{{task_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Check currentReservationId here after enqueuing/webhook-posting a task -- if your agent was Available, it should already be matched. Copy that into {{reservation_id}} (or use 'List Agent Pending Offers')."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Agent Pending Offers (post-match)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.reservations && body.reservations.length > 0) { pm.collectionVariables.set('reservation_id', body.reservations[0].reservationId); }",
                  "pm.test('at least one pending offer for this agent', () => { pm.expect(body.reservations && body.reservations.length).to.be.above(0); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/agents/{{agent_id}}/offers",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "agents",
                "{{agent_id}}",
                "offers"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-checks offers after task creation/matching (folder 3's copy of this same call ran before any task existed, so it was always empty). Captures {{reservation_id}} for Accept/Reject Reservation below. {{agent_id}} must still be Available and hold this queue/channel -- run folders 1-3 first without deleting the agent."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Accept Reservation",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/reservations/{{reservation_id}}/accept",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "reservations",
                "{{reservation_id}}",
                "accept"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.AcceptReservation."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Complete Task",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/tasks/{{task_id}}/complete",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "tasks",
                "{{task_id}}",
                "complete"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Required auth. TaskRouterService.CompleteTask. Publishes task.completed -- Historical Reporting durably ingests this; Background Worker Pool durably consumes it to trigger a wrap-up sync job (see GAPS.md for that pipeline's known simplifications)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Dashboard",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/dashboard",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "dashboard"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Digital Channels Gateway",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Inbound Chat Webhook",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.taskId) { pm.collectionVariables.set('task_id', body.taskId); }",
                  "pm.test('201 and taskId present', () => { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(201); pm.expect(body.taskId).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{dcg_base}}/webhooks/chat/{{tenant_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{dcg_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "chat",
                "{{tenant_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"postman-session-1\",\n  \"from\": \"+15551234567\",\n  \"text\": \"Hi, I need help\",\n  \"queue_id\": \"{{queue_id}}\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "NOT via API Gateway -- direct to Digital Channels Gateway, a different trust boundary (see ARCHITECTURE_FLOW.md §4.2). Deliberately unauthenticated this milestone (no signature/secret verification) -- see GAPS.md's 'Digital Channels Gateway webhook has no signature/secret verification' entry, and services/digital-channels-gateway/internal/webhookapi's ServeHTTP doc comment for the full tradeoff. \n\nThis is 'create a chat interaction' -- the end-to-end path from an inbound message to a real Task Router Task."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "6. API Gateway - WebSocket Ticket",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Mint WS Ticket",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.ticket) { pm.collectionVariables.set('ws_ticket', body.ticket); }",
                  "pm.test('200 and ticket present', () => { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.equal(200); pm.expect(body.ticket).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{api_gateway_base}}/v1/ws-ticket",
              "host": [
                "{{api_gateway_base}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "ws-ticket"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Required auth (normal session bearer token). Gateway-local -- not a backend RPC. Mints a short-lived (~45s) ticket for a browser client that can't set a custom Authorization header on a WebSocket upgrade. See services/api-gateway/internal/wsticket's doc comment for the short-TTL-not-single-use tradeoff (also in GAPS.md).\n\nAfter running this, open ws://localhost:18080/ws?ticket={{ws_ticket}} in a WebSocket client (Postman's WebSocket Request type, or wscat) WITHIN ~45 seconds. Requires kubectl port-forward svc/api-gateway-svc 18080:8080 (already assumed) since the proxy lives on API Gateway's HTTP port, not a separate one."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Cleanup & Alternate Paths (standalone)",
      "description": "Destructive requests, deliberately isolated from the default sequential 1-through-5 flow. Run these ONLY after you are done exercising folders 1-5 against a given tenant, or standalone when testing admin-registry deletion specifically. Running any of these mid-sequence will break later requests that depend on the resource being removed. Also holds Reject Reservation -- an alternate path to Accept Reservation (folder 4), not a follow-on step; a reservation can only be accepted OR rejected, not both.",
